        "original_id": "5a99bdb9-77a6-5ad2-a835-1cd0a58afe73",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John O'Hara, Rabindranath Tagore\n- Roles: writer, polymath\n- Topics: social realism, social status and manners, Bengali literature, Bengali music, Indian art, Contextual Modernism\n\nFacts:\n- Rabindranath Tagore was born on 7 May 1861 and died on 7 August 1941.\n- Rabindranath Tagore was a Bengali polymath with the sobriquet Gurudev and the honorific FRAS.\n- In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, Rabindranath Tagore reshaped Bengali literature and music and Indian art through Contextual Modernism.\n- John Henry O'Hara was born on January 31, 1905 and died on April 11, 1970.\n- John O'Hara was an American writer.\n- John O'Hara was best remembered as a keen observer of social status and manners in early to mid 20th-century America.\n- John O'Hara was regarded as pre-eminent among his contemporaries in depicting social realism.",
